The net cash provided from financing activities for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 was primarily related to capital contributions from Southern Company and net issuance of senior notes, partially offset by common stock dividend payments, a reduction in commercial paper borrowings, and net distributions to noncontrolling interests.

Net cash provided from operating activities increased $147 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 as compared to the corresponding period in 2025 primarily due to increased billings, the timing of customer receivable collections, and higher natural gas cost recovery as a result of higher natural gas prices, partially offset by higher volumes of natural gas purchases and the timing of payments for natural gas.

The net cash used for investing activities for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 was primarily related to construction of transmission and distribution assets recovered through base rates.

The net cash used for financing activities for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 was primarily related to common stock dividend payments, a reduction in commercial paper borrowings, and maturities of first mortgage bonds, partially offset by the issuance of junior subordinated notes and the net issuance of senior notes.

